# alpine_route.words - SLAM 450 Flight Planner v0.1: the alpine route's
# waypoints, Sydney Heads to Port Melbourne over Mt Kosciuszko.
# point|name|lat|lon   (degrees, south and west negative)
# Hume Highway to Goulburn, then Bungendore and the Monaro to Cooma, up the
# Kosciuszko Road through Jindabyne, Perisher and Charlotte Pass to the
# summit (2,228 m), down to Thredbo, the Alpine Way past Tom Groggin to
# Khancoban, then Corryong, Albury and the Hume Highway to Melbourne.
# Straight legs between towns; ground between waypoints is not yet seen
# (Copernicus DEM, a later phase). Airspace not yet checked: Bungendore
# passes east of Canberra, Albury has a tower, Broadmeadows is under
# Melbourne's control zone.
# Route: Tom Dyer ("quick deviation around Mt Kosciuszko", 8 Nov 2026).
# Written by Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-08.
